  "imagery": "King County GIS, KingCo_Aerial_2025",
  "imagery_note": "0.101 m/px at Seattle's latitude -- USABLE but coarser than Denver's 0.057, so a ramp is ~15 px rather than ~26 and the measured offset floor is roughly twice Denver's. Adequate for sizing a LARGE error, which is what the Poor anchor needs; it would not be adequate for grading a city expected to be Good. 2025 is the most current year King County publishes, matching an inventory filtered to actively-maintained ramps.",
